## Verdict

The obstruction that kept the theorem on the star turns out to
have been a misreading of its own preparation: the non-uniformity
runs along each arm, not across them, and symmetry never cared
about the direction the theorem feared. With the reduction
extended, the lane's most stubborn small mystery — why arm length
never mattered — resolves into two clean pieces: an exact lemma
saying the arms' own energies are invisible to every singular
value, and a ladder saying each deeper site pays another two
powers of the field to be heard, graded by depth alone. The chain
that began this lane's geometry story as an impossibility, and
survived every law since as the one exception, ends it as an
ordinary citizen: two arms, one spider, fourteen digits. The
theorem now knows exactly where it lives — every symmetric-armed
creature in, one asymmetric witness and the loopy family out, and
one lemma quietly reaching across the border. Independent audit
still required.
